--------------------- CableDyn Input File ------------------------------------
CableDyn driver deck -- chain-polyester-chain mooring with a mesh-independent axial damping ratio, Airy wave, 60 s
-- The three-section mooring of composite_chain_poly_chain.dat (200 m depth) under a regular
-- 4 m, 10 s Airy wave, ramped in over 10 s. Every section's BA is -0.02, and the OPTION
-- axialDampingRatio mode1 reads a negative BA as the damping ratio of the line's first axial
-- mode (both ends held), worked out from the sections' lengths, EA and dry mass: here 2 % at
-- 2.03 Hz on any mesh. Each element then takes BA = 2 zeta EA/omega1, a damping
-- proportional to the stiffness, which damps axial mode n at zeta omega_n/omega_1. Under the
-- default segment form the same -0.02 would damp the first mode at about zeta pi/(2N) = 0.04 %
-- on these 77 elements, and half that on a mesh twice as fine.
